{
  "headline": "FDA's records trace our supply to a plant classified OAI 150 days before the posting",
  "headline_cites": ["D16"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA first posted the atropine sulfate shortage on 2012-01-01 and it remains Current as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["E51", "D20"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The product used at Corvale General and Corvale East (NDC 00409163010) is labeled by Hospira, Inc. and manufactured at FEI 1021343.",
      "cites": ["E4", "E1", "E21"]
    },
    {
      "text": "FDA inspected that plant on 2011-08-04 and classified it OAI with 483 observations for laboratory controls and written procedures, 150 days before the shortage posting.",
      "cites": ["E15", "D16"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Earlier inspections of the same plant were also classified OAI on 2010-01-19 (712 days before posting) and 2011-03-15 (292 days before posting).",
      "cites": ["E11", "D11", "D14"]
    },
    {
      "text": "A Warning Letter was issued to the plant on 2011-08-31, 123 days before the posting.",
      "cites": ["E20", "D17"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 1.8 days of the 0.1 mg/mL 10 mL syringe on hand while Corvale General has 16.5 days.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The rule‑ranked option is to transfer 10 syringes of 0.1 mg/mL, 10 mL from Corvale General to Corvale East, which would give Corvale East about 5 days of supply.",
      "cites": ["D21"]
    }
  ]
}
